  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). Both defects real; defect 1's stated consequence is WRONG, defect 2 is WORSE than stated. Keep P2.\n- DEFECT 1 CORRECTION: the missing DictWriter rows do NOT let a host_fs claim read confirmed. module_io_is_enumerated matches exactly (io_boundary.py ~1292-1362), so the \"csv: complete\" grant does not cover the csv.DictWriter slot. Repro def dump(f): t=os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]; dw=csv.DictWriter(f,...); dw.writeheader(); dw.writerow({\"a\":t}) with host_secret->host_fs gives INCONCLUSIVE (rc 2), \"could not classify (csv.DictWriter)\". The cost is a lost finding with the verdict withheld (the safe direction), and the complete declaration is not at fault.\n- DEFECT 2 IS A FALSE CLEAN: def dump(w): t=os.environ[...]; w.writerow([t]) with def main(f): w=csv.writer(f); dump(w) gives CONFIRMED_WITH_CAVEATS (rc 3), only the unknown_receiver_scope caveat on writerow. When csv.writer(f) is in the same function it reads violated, only because ddg_mixed flags the constructor call.\n- FIX-SHAPE NOTE: py.py:702 _derive_external_constructor_types derives receiver types from dotted kind:method rows, so rowing csv.DictWriter.{writerow,writerows,writeheader} should type DictWriter receivers with no other work. csv.writer is a lowercase function and still needs a return-type declaration, as stated.\n- Unchanged since filing: python.yaml:453 (csv writer row), python.yaml:1616 (csv complete); no csv entry in library_signatures/python.yaml.\n- NOT CHECKED: whether library_signatures can express a module-function return type that py.py consumes for a bare module call."  # 3511
